config DEFY_LIGHTING
    bool "Defy half lighting and host feedback"
    default y
    depends on DEFY_HYBRID && SETTINGS
    select DEFY_CONTROL
    select CRC if ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      The halves' lighting and its controls, with the looks and layer
      colours the keymap sets, the overlay that shows the selected Bluetooth
      profile and output on the halves' keys, and the Bluetooth profile
      chooser. See docs/lighting.md.

config DEFY_HALF_LEDS
    bool "A half's LED interface"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_DYGMA_DEFY_LEDS_ENABLED
    select LED_STRIP
    help
      Everything a half shows on its LEDs: how far its start-up got, from
      ZMK running through the radio firmware install to Bluetooth and the
      link to the Neuron, a report when the radio fails, and the displays
      the Neuron asks for: the lighting state, the battery display's cells, the
      host overlay and the profile chooser. The half's own low-battery
      warning shows there too. See docs/lighting.md. ZMK's RGB underglow
      must stay off, as it drives the same LEDs.
